 ('ENT_SAM_MOSES','PER_SAMARITAN','In Samaritan theology Moses is the unsurpassable prophet, sole revealer of the complete Torah, sometimes given pre-cosmic dignity in Memar Marqah; no later prophet is canonical. Homonym/reception of the Israelite Moses (ENT_ISR_MOSES).'),
 ('ENT_SAM_TAHEB','PER_SAMARITAN','The Taheb (''the one who returns/restores'') is the Samaritan messianic figure, a prophet like Moses (Deut 18:18) who will restore true worship on Gerizim and the hidden cult vessels; attested in Samaritan sources and discussed by Pummer and Anderson-Giles. Functional analogue of the Jewish Messiah.'),
 ('ENT_SAM_MARQAH','PER_SAMARITAN','4th-c. CE Samaritan theologian, traditional author of the Memar Marqah (Tibat Marqe) and liturgical poems; the great systematizer of Samaritan theology of Moses and the Glory. Historical figure.'),
 ('ENT_SAM_BABA_RABBA','PER_SAMARITAN','4th-c. CE Samaritan reformer who reorganized the community, established sages/hukama and synagogue worship, traditionally associated with a Samaritan revival; historical figure attested in the Samaritan chronicles and Anderson-Giles.'),
 ('ENT_SAM_HIGH_PRIEST','PER_SAMARITAN','The hereditary Samaritan high priesthood, claimed from Aaron/Levi via Phinehas (and after that line''s end, from the Levitical line of Uzziel); the living head of the community on Gerizim. Continuous office, well attested.'),
 ('ENT_SAM_PHINEHAS','PER_SAMARITAN','Phinehas son of Eleazar son of Aaron is venerated as the zealous priest and ancestor of the Samaritan high-priestly line (the ''Pinhasite'' priesthood). Pentateuchal figure read through Samaritan priestly genealogy.'),
 ('ENT_SAM_GERIZIM','PER_SAMARITAN','Mount Gerizim is the Samaritan ''chosen place'' (the tenth commandment in the Samaritan Decalogue), site of the temple/altar, the Passover sacrifice, and the eschatological restoration; the central sacred realm of the religion. Archaeologically and textually attested.'),
 ('ENT_SAM_GLORY','PER_SAMARITAN','Samaritan theology (esp. Memar Marqah) develops the divine Glory/Light (the Kavod) as God''s manifestation at Sinai and upon Moses'' face; a mediating presence akin to but distinct from the Jewish Shekhinah/Kavod. Attested in Marqah.'),
 ('ENT_SAM_ANGEL','PER_SAMARITAN','Samaritan theology recognizes the Angel/Malak as a created mediator of God''s word and presence (e.g., the Angel at the burning bush and Sinai), within a strictly monotheistic framework; discussed in Pummer and Memar Marqah.'),
 ('ENT_SAM_TORAH','PER_SAMARITAN','The Samaritan Pentateuch (Samaritan Hebrew Torah) is the entire Samaritan canon, with distinctive readings (notably the Gerizim commandment); the Abisha Scroll is its most venerated copy. Well attested textual tradition.'),
 ('ENT_SAM_PASSOVER','PER_SAMARITAN','The living Samaritan Passover sacrifice on Mount Gerizim is the most distinctive surviving Israelite blood-sacrifice; publicly attested annual ritual. Modeled only at the level of public observance, not ritual interiors.'),
 ('ENT_SAM_JOSEPH','PER_SAMARITAN','Samaritans identify principally as descendants of Joseph through Ephraim and Manasseh (the ''B''nei Yosef''); Joseph and Gerizim/Shechem are central to their self-understanding. Reception of the Pentateuchal Joseph (ENT_ISR_JOSEPH).'),
 ('ENT_SAM_JOSHUA','PER_SAMARITAN','In Samaritan tradition (incl. the Samaritan Book of Joshua/Chronicle) Joshua leads Israel into the land and establishes the sanctuary at Gerizim near Shechem, inaugurating the period of Divine Favor (Rahuta). Reception of the Israelite Joshua (ENT_ISR_JOSHUA).'),
 ('ENT_SAM_RAHUTA_FANUTA','PER_SAMARITAN','Samaritan periodization of sacred history into Rahuta (the era of divine Favor, from Moses/Joshua) and Fanuta (the era of divine Disfavor/turning-away, beginning with Eli''s schism), to be ended by the Taheb. Attested in Samaritan chronicles and Pummer.');
INSERT INTO entity_periods (entity_id,period_id,confidence,rationale,source_id,review_status)
INSERT INTO _r VALUES
 ('ENT_SAM_SHEMA','member_of','ENT_SAM_PANTHEON','high','The one God of the Samaritans is the central object of the tradition''s worship; placed in the cohort hub.'),
 ('ENT_SAM_MOSES','member_of','ENT_SAM_PANTHEON','high','Moses, the supreme Samaritan prophet, is a core member of the cohort.'),
 ('ENT_SAM_TAHEB','member_of','ENT_SAM_PANTHEON','high','The Taheb is the Samaritan eschatological figure within the cohort.'),
 ('ENT_SAM_MARQAH','member_of','ENT_SAM_PANTHEON','high','Marqah is the foundational Samaritan theologian in the cohort.'),
 ('ENT_SAM_BABA_RABBA','member_of','ENT_SAM_PANTHEON','high','Baba Rabba, the reformer, belongs to the Samaritan cohort.'),
 ('ENT_SAM_HIGH_PRIEST','member_of','ENT_SAM_PANTHEON','high','The high-priestly office is a core institution of the cohort.'),
 ('ENT_SAM_PHINEHAS','member_of','ENT_SAM_PANTHEON','high','Phinehas, ancestor of the priestly line, belongs to the cohort.'),
 ('ENT_SAM_GERIZIM','member_of','ENT_SAM_PANTHEON','high','Mount Gerizim, the sacred realm, anchors the cohort.'),
 ('ENT_SAM_GLORY','member_of','ENT_SAM_PANTHEON','high','The divine Glory is a theological concept within the cohort.'),
 ('ENT_SAM_ANGEL','member_of','ENT_SAM_PANTHEON','high','The Angel/Malak belongs to the Samaritan cohort.'),
 ('ENT_SAM_TORAH','member_of','ENT_SAM_PANTHEON','high','The Samaritan Torah is the canon of the cohort.'),
 ('ENT_SAM_PASSOVER','member_of','ENT_SAM_PANTHEON','high','The Gerizim Passover sacrifice is a core ritual of the cohort.'),
 ('ENT_SAM_JOSEPH','member_of','ENT_SAM_PANTHEON','high','Joseph, ancestor of the Samaritans, belongs to the cohort.'),
 ('ENT_SAM_JOSHUA','member_of','ENT_SAM_PANTHEON','high','Joshua, who founded Gerizim worship, belongs to the cohort.'),
 ('ENT_SAM_RAHUTA_FANUTA','member_of','ENT_SAM_PANTHEON','high','The Rahuta/Fanuta periodization is a cosmological concept of the cohort.'),
 ('ENT_SAM_MOSES','reveals','ENT_SAM_TORAH','high','In Samaritan theology Moses is the sole revealer of the complete Torah.'),
 ('ENT_SAM_MARQAH','transmits','ENT_SAM_TORAH','medium','Marqah''s Memar Marqah is the foundational theological exposition transmitting Samaritan Torah doctrine.'),
 ('ENT_SAM_MARQAH','reveals','ENT_SAM_GLORY','medium','Marqah''s Memar Marqah develops the doctrine of the divine Glory/Light upon Moses.'),
 ('ENT_SAM_GLORY','emanates_from','ENT_SAM_SHEMA','medium','The Glory is God''s own manifest presence/Light proceeding from the one God.'),
 ('ENT_SAM_ANGEL','mediates','ENT_SAM_SHEMA','medium','The created Angel/Malak mediates God''s word and presence in Samaritan theology.'),
 ('ENT_SAM_GLORY','revealed_by','ENT_SAM_MOSES','medium','The Glory shone upon and was made manifest through Moses at Sinai per Memar Marqah.'),
 ('ENT_SAM_HIGH_PRIEST','presides_over','ENT_SAM_PASSOVER','high','The Samaritan high priest presides over the annual Passover sacrifice on Gerizim.'),
 ('ENT_SAM_PASSOVER','dwells_in','ENT_SAM_GERIZIM','high','The Samaritan Passover sacrifice is performed on Mount Gerizim, the chosen place.'),
 ('ENT_SAM_HIGH_PRIEST','child_of','ENT_SAM_PHINEHAS','medium','The Samaritan high-priestly line is traced from Phinehas (the Pinhasite priesthood).'),
 ('ENT_SAM_JOSHUA','presides_over','ENT_SAM_GERIZIM','medium','In Samaritan tradition Joshua established the sanctuary on Gerizim, inaugurating the Rahuta.'),
 ('ENT_SAM_JOSHUA','participates_in_creation','ENT_SAM_RAHUTA_FANUTA','low','Joshua''s establishment of Gerizim worship inaugurates the era of divine Favor (Rahuta).'),
 ('ENT_SAM_BABA_RABBA','member_of','ENT_SAM_HIGH_PRIEST','low','Baba Rabba operated in close concert with the priesthood in reorganizing the community.'),
 ('ENT_SAM_TAHEB','eschatological_role','ENT_SAM_GERIZIM','medium','The Taheb is expected to restore true worship and recover the hidden vessels on Mount Gerizim.'),
 ('ENT_SAM_TAHEB','reception_of','ENT_SAM_MOSES','medium','The Taheb is understood as the prophet like Moses (Deut 18:18) who restores Mosaic worship.'),
 ('ENT_SAM_MOSES','reception_of','ENT_ISR_MOSES','high','The Samaritan supreme prophet Moses is a tradition-specific reception of the Israelite Moses; same scriptural figure, distinct theological elevation. Homonym across traditions.'),
 ('ENT_SAM_JOSHUA','reception_of','ENT_ISR_JOSHUA','high','Samaritan Joshua (builder of the Gerizim altar) receives the Israelite Joshua. Homonym.'),
 ('ENT_SAM_JOSEPH','reception_of','ENT_ISR_JOSEPH','high','Samaritans claim descent through Joseph (Ephraim/Manasseh); their Joseph is a reception of the Pentateuchal Joseph. Homonym.'),
 ('ENT_SAM_PHINEHAS','child_of','ENT_ISR_AARON','medium','Phinehas son of Eleazar son of Aaron; the Samaritan priestly line descends from Aaron via Phinehas. Linked to the existing Israelite Aaron.'),
 ('ENT_SAM_SHEMA','equated_with','ENT_ISR_YAHWEH','high','The one God of the Samaritans is the same God of Israel (Yahweh/the tetragrammaton); a shared Israelite deity worshipped under a distinct Gerizim cult.'),
 ('ENT_SAM_TAHEB','aligned_with','ENT_ISL_MUSA','low','The Taheb expectation as a returning prophet-like-Moses functionally aligns with the prophet-of-restoration role; modern cross-tradition functional alignment, not identity.'),
 ('ENT_SAM_GLORY','aligned_with','ENT_JM_SHEKHINAH','medium','The Samaritan divine Glory/Kavod is a functional cognate of the Jewish Shekhinah/Kavod as God''s manifest presence; parallel mediating concepts in sister Israelite traditions (modern comparative alignment, not identity).');
